{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9183","id":4541886282,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABDrevSg","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9183","diff_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9183.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9183.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9183","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9183/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9183/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9183/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/statuses/95dafae39c20c55b8078f911a8656d9e1c24b22b","number":9183,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[grug] Launch the QuACK grouped GEMMs without PDL","user":{"login":"mcwitt","id":319411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTQxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The three QuACK grouped-GEMM launchers in `quack_moe_cute` now pass `use_pdl=False`, so the gated, plain, and weight-gradient kernels start after the preceding kernel completes instead of overlapping it under programmatic dependent launch.\n\nQuACK 0.6.4's SM100 GEMM executes `griddepcontrol.wait` only in its TMA-load and CLC-scheduler warps. The MMA and epilogue warps decode their work tiles from `cu_seqlens` in global memory before any wait, so a PDL-launched GEMM can read the expert group boundaries before the previous kernel's writes are visible. Both GPU dumps of the ragged EP hero hang (#8870, steps 107501 and 108711) show that split: in every stuck CTA the MMA and epilogue warps retired on a tile the load and scheduler warps still held as valid, and one cluster retired on its first tile. The load warp then blocks on the A/B pipeline and the rank never reaches the next ragged all-to-all barrier.\n\nCost was measured on the six-GEMM expert MLP forward and backward at the hero shape (601,088 rows, 6 experts, hidden 6144, intermediate 3072) on two GB200 nodes, 1,000 iterations per arm, each arm twice per GPU: median 87.6 ms per iteration with PDL off against 87.7 ms with PDL on on one node, 88.7 ms against 88.5 ms on the other, within 0.3% and inside the per-GPU spread. 32,000 iterations ran without a hang or non-finite value.\n\nThe change is a mitigation. Neither probe reproduced the hang in 100,000 launches, and the hero rate is about one hang per 1e6 GPU-steps, so the change is judged by the recurrence interval on the next hero relaunch. The probes and their per-arm results are recorded on the issue. The upstream fix is a `griddepcontrol.wait` in QuACK's MMA and epilogue warps, which one probe arm exercised with a patched copy of QuACK.\n\nPart of #8870\n","labels":[{"id":10166074947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACXfH-Qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agent-generated","name":"agent-generated","description":"Created by automation/agent","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null